  "readings": [
    "The few-epoch question is read only where the arms a reading uses were still improving their validation loss from E2 to E3 (NOT_OVERFIT). The models are small (depth 4, at most 34.7 M parameters) and this is one corpus family at one recipe. No reading claims a mechanism or a scaling law.",
    "At 3e-4 at E3, p* at 512 is above p* at 384 and at 768 on fresh draws (INTERIOR_PEAK). This is an ordering of three rungs; it does not place the peak between rungs.",
    "Peak at 3e-4 only (RATE_DEPENDENT): at 1e-4, 768 is above 512, so the fall seen at 3e-4 is rate-dependent, at the two rates tested.",
    "D3, a pre-registered secondary: p* at 512 at 3e-4 minus p* at 768 at 1e-4, at E3. It is not a test of the rate account, because it compares two rates. Stated in advance: on t00 the gap at 512 at 3e-4 (0.5676) is above the gap at 768 at 1e-4 (0.5382), so if p* simply tracked the gap, D3 would be above 0 with no turn at 768.",
    "Data: never-assigned WikiText-103 training articles, with text duplicates of assigned articles and repeats inside the pool removed; new seeds; no new tuning. The validation set, the pre-training pool and the tokenizer are those of the earlier natural-text studies. The hypothesis was formed after seeing d01-d10, and the idea for the control also came after seeing p*; the rate 1e-4 comes from validation NLL on t00 only."
  ],
